{lo ka ta pelxu} is clearly grammatical.=A0 the problem is that (like most =
things that are grammatical) it doesn't make any obvious sense or, perhaps,=
 makes too many not very obvious senses.=A0 A property of worlds, say, or a=
 particular shade of yellow in this one or ... .=A0 How is it to be avoided=
 ? Allowing only {ce'u} after {ka}?=A0 And thus creating a new word class -=
-or two?=A0 Seems Draconian, when you can get by by just not using it.

Be nice to know what version of xorlo Lojbab understands.




